Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:50:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Claim combat-damage events once their triggers are collected
 (CR 603.2c)

The combat-damage step collects the abilities its events trigger. The
post-action scan skipped those events only when the batch reached the stack;
behind an ordering or target prompt the stack is still empty and an ordinary
ability beside a delayed one was collected a second time.

The claim covers the step's own events only (the damage batch and the
state-based actions after it). Earlier events of the same pass, such as life
lost to unspent mana when the previous step ended, were not scanned by the
step and stay visible to the post-action scan.

